From 965317d4362cd4efbede12f2a0bbc4ffe83d6044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Wed, 25 Feb 2026 10:54:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Unihertz 8849 hardware controls

Add a settings menu for the Unihertz 8849 (Tank) device-specific
hardware, detected via the Agold HAL and FPGA sysfs interface.

Features:
- Warning light: Off/Red/Blue/Green/SOS modes (ioctl 310)
  SOS is app-driven red/blue alternating flash at ~3Hz
- Camping light: Off/Full/Medium/Low/Flash/SOS modes (ioctl 301)
  Full brightness auto-steps down to medium after configurable
  duration (5/10/15/30 min) to prevent overheating
- Projector enable/disable matching stock powerOnOffForPrejectorOn/Off
  sequence: display resize, AoD disable, sleep/wake via PowerManager,
  ioctl 500 sub-commands (0,4 / 0,6 / mode / 0,3), calibration
- Projector mode selection (portrait, landscape, landscape inverted)
- Phone display toggle while projecting
- Brightness slider (1-255) with live value display
- Auto-keystone always on: exact replica of stock calculateOrientation
  (10-sample accumulation, 3s cycle, GSI sign correction)
- Temperature-reactive fan control matching stock ElephantProduct
  (start 20%, ramp to 30% at >40C, 100% at >48C, gradual delta)
- Per-device factory focus calibration from proinfo partition
- Laser distance readout updating every second while in settings

The Agold daemon can restart after ioctl calls causing DeadObjectException
on stale binders. sendCalibration() retries up to 5 times with backoff,
and sendIoctl() retries once, ensuring calibration is always delivered.

Removed: manual keystone, focus calibration/adjust, fan override,
projector temperature display (all handled automatically).

Sysfs writes use direct File I/O, requiring the companion SELinux
policy patch (sysfs_fpga_spi type, system_app rw_file_perms).
